{
 "openapi": "3.0.3",
 "info": {
  "title": "Freya Bank voice assistant: statement and debt services",
  "version": "2026-10-01",
  "description": "The seven services the voice assistant calls, from the 1 Oct 2026 service contract (Mert Koç). The OAuth2 token call (POST https://api.freyabank.example/oauth2/token) is left out: it is not a phone-agent tool, and the test environment does not check the token or headers. Every service is POST, JSON in and out, UTF-8. Success = HTTP 200 and result.returnCode \"1\". Dates are dd.MM.yyyy strings. Amounts are JSON numbers with a dot decimal and must not be rounded."
 },
 "servers": [
  {
   "url": "https://api.freyabank.example/voice/v1/"
  }
 ],
 "x-conflicts": [
  "Card number masking: the service contract (5.1, 1 Oct) says test cards.list returns first 6 + last 4 and that production is unconfirmed. Selin's 9 Oct decisions-recap mail says production cards.list returns the full number. The 8 Oct and 2 Sep analyses say the services return masked numbers. Contract followed: cardNumber is an opaque string, sent back exactly as cards.list returned it.",
  "cards.balance cardNumber masking: the contract (5.2) and test-customers.md say the balance answer is masked first 4 + last 4 (5400********1234). The 2 Sep analysis §8 says cards.list and cards.balance both show the first six and last four.",
  "customerNo type: the cards.list example sends a string and the contact.email.get example sends a number. The contract and test-customers.md accept both.",
  "newStatementWeek: the contract accepts a number or a string, and test-customers.md uses \"1\"..\"4\" keys. statement.week.change returns statementWeek and statementDay as strings, while other services return numbers.",
  "Due-date field name: statement.week.decide uses statementDueDate, while cards.balance and statement.week.get use lastPayDate (contract 5.4).",
  "Statement-week change limits: the IVR prompt sheet (10 Sep, STW-091/092) says once a month and three times a year. The FAQ (14 Aug 2025) says up to three times a year. Kerem (7 Oct transcript, 8 Oct analysis §7) says once per calendar year for the assistant channel. No service exposes whether the change right is still available (contract 5.3, open point 3).",
  "E-mail target: the FAQ (2025) says a statement can be e-mailed to any address. The contract (5.7) says the backend sends to whatever address is in emailAddress and does not check it. Selin (24-29 Sep mails, 8 Oct analysis §6) says only the registered address.",
  "Which statement: the FAQ says statements from the last 12 months are downloadable in the app. The analyses say the assistant sends only the last cut statement (statementDate from cards.balance).",
  "Second factor: the call-flow PDF shows a 'Second factor needed?' box. The mails (Selin, Burcu 28 Sep) and the 8 Oct analysis say it was never built and the assistant does no identity check.",
  "New card without a statement: the 10 Oct transcript says statementDate and lastPayDate come back empty for that card. The contract states dates as dd.MM.yyyy strings.",
  "Missing records in the test environment: the contract (§6) and test-customers.md say to return that service's 404 from section 4, or 400 INVALID_ARGUMENTS_ERROR where the service has no 404. statement.week.get, decide and change, contact.email.get and statement.pdf.send for unknown entries follow this. test-customers.md says some customers have no statement.pdf.send entry, and that service's 404 is FB_IVR_CHANNEL_107.",
  "Timeouts: no client timeout is agreed (contract 4 and 7.1). One test entry has delaySeconds and an answer can take more than 10 s and still succeed. The contract suggests no automatic retry on statement.week.change or statement.pdf.send.",
  "401 errors: the contract lists 401 (gateway) for all services in the error table, but only for statement.week.change in its per-service list. It defines no 401 body.",
  "cards.list 400 INVALID_ARGUMENTS_ERROR is listed for 'all' services in the error table, but is not repeated in the per-service error lists for cards.list and statement.week.get."
 ],
 "paths": {
  "/cards.list": {
   "post": {
    "operationId": "cards.list",
    "summary": "The customer's cards the assistant may talk about",
    "requestBody": {
     "required": true,
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
         "data"
        ],
        "properties": {
         "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "customerNo"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "customerNo": {
            "oneOf": [
             {
              "type": "string"
             },
             {
              "type": "integer"
             }
            ],
            "description": "\"customerNo may be sent as a string or as a number, both are accepted.\""
           },
           "aiFlow": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
             "CardOps"
            ],
            "description": "\"aiFlow tells us which use case is asking; for this one it's \\\"CardOps\\\" (not validated in test).\""
           }
          }
         },
         "call": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CallMeta"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "description": "Success",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": [
          "data",
          "result"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "data": {
           "type": "object",
           "properties": {
            "cards": {
             "type": "array",
             "description": "Only active cards come back.",
             "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
               "cardNumber": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "\"always send the cardNumber exactly as cards.list returned it\"; masked 540000******1234 in test."
               },
               "cardNumberLast4": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Last four digits; \"Don't assume cardNumberLast4 is unique.\""
               },
               "productName": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "\"free text from the card system\"; may be empty."
               },
               "status": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                 "A"
                ],
                "description": "\"Only active cards come back (status \\\"A\\\").\""
               },
               "isMainCard": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "\"false for a card that isn't the customer's own main card; it's still in the list.\""
               }
              }
             }
            },
            "validCardsCount": {
             "type": "integer",
             "description": "Number of valid cards."
            },
            "exitState": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "1_CARD",
              "MULTI_CARD"
             ],
             "description": "\"exitState: \\\"1_CARD\\\" or \\\"MULTI_CARD\\\".\""
            }
           }
          },
          "result": {
           "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Result"
          }
         }
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "400": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/InvalidArguments"
     },
     "401": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
     },
     "404": {
      "description": "FB_IVR_CHANNEL_102 WARNING: \"Müşteriye ait geçerli kart bilgisi bulunamadı.\" (no eligible card, not a broken service)",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "500": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/TechnicalError"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "/cards.balance": {
   "post": {
    "operationId": "cards.balance",
    "summary": "Statement and due dates, debt per currency for one card",
    "requestBody": {
     "required": true,
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
         "data"
        ],
        "properties": {
         "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "cardNumber"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "cardNumber": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "\"always send the cardNumber exactly as cards.list returned it\"."
           }
          }
         },
         "call": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CallMeta"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "description": "Success",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": [
          "data",
          "result"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "data": {
           "type": "object",
           "properties": {
            "cardNumber": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "\"masked differently from the card list (first 4 + last 4 ...). Don't use it to match against the list\"."
            },
            "cardNumberLast4": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Last four digits of the card."
            },
            "productName": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Card product name."
            },
            "statementDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "\"the last issued statement\" date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "lastPayDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Due date of the last issued statement, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "nextStatementDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "\"the coming\" statement date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "nextLastPayDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "The coming due date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "debtTL": {
             "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DebtBlock"
            },
            "debtUSD": {
             "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DebtBlock"
            },
            "debtEUR": {
             "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DebtBlock"
            },
            "debtGBP": {
             "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DebtBlock"
            },
            "statementPaymentStatus": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "HAS_DEBT",
              "NO_DEBT"
             ],
             "description": "Card-overall statement status."
            },
            "totalDebtPaymentStatus": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "HAS_DEBT",
              "NO_DEBT"
             ],
             "description": "Card-overall total-debt status."
            },
            "automaticPaymentFlag": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "Y",
              "N"
             ],
             "description": "\"automaticPaymentFlag: \\\"Y\\\" / \\\"N\\\".\""
            }
           },
           "description": "\"A block can be missing (some cards have no GBP block at all). Missing block is not the same as a block with NO_DEBT; don't invent zeros for it.\""
          },
          "result": {
           "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Result"
          }
         }
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "400": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/InvalidArguments"
     },
     "401": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
     },
     "404": {
      "description": "FB_IVR_CHANNEL_120 WARNING: card not found",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "500": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/TechnicalError"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "/statement.week.get": {
   "post": {
    "operationId": "statement.week.get",
    "summary": "The card's current statement week and day, joint statement info",
    "requestBody": {
     "required": true,
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
         "data"
        ],
        "properties": {
         "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "cardNumber"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "cardNumber": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Card number exactly as cards.list returned it."
           }
          }
         },
         "call": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CallMeta"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "description": "Success",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": [
          "data",
          "result"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "data": {
           "type": "object",
           "properties": {
            "cardNumber": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Masked card number (first 6 + last 4 in test)."
            },
            "cardNumberLast4": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Last four digits."
            },
            "productName": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Card product name."
            },
            "statementWeek": {
             "type": "integer",
             "minimum": 1,
             "maximum": 4,
             "description": "\"1 to 4, the week of the month the statement is cut.\""
            },
            "statementDay": {
             "type": "integer",
             "description": "\"day of the month\"."
            },
            "statementDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Statement date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "lastPayDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Due date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "nextStatementDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Next statement date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "nextLastPayDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "Next due date, dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "relationType": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "",
              "M",
              "C"
             ],
             "description": "\"empty string when the card has its own statement. \\\"M\\\" or \\\"C\\\" when two cards share one statement\" (M = main, C = linked)."
            },
            "relatedCardNumber": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "The other card on a shared statement; otherwise empty string."
            },
            "relatedCardProductName": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "The other card's name on a shared statement; otherwise empty string."
            }
           }
          },
          "result": {
           "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Result"
          }
         }
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "400": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/InvalidArguments"
     },
     "401": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
     },
     "404": {
      "description": "FB_IVR_CHANNEL_121 WARNING: card not found",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "500": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/TechnicalError"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "/statement.week.decide": {
   "post": {
    "operationId": "statement.week.decide",
    "summary": "Preview of the dates with a requested week; changes nothing",
    "requestBody": {
     "required": true,
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
         "data"
        ],
        "properties": {
         "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "cardNumber",
           "newStatementWeek",
           "statementDay"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "cardNumber": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Card number exactly as cards.list returned it."
           },
           "newStatementWeek": {
            "oneOf": [
             {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 4
             },
             {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
               "1",
               "2",
               "3",
               "4"
              ]
             }
            ],
            "description": "\"1-4, number or string both fine.\" Not the card's current week (\"you'll get an error\")."
           },
           "statementDay": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "\"the card's current statementDay from statement.week.get.\""
           }
          }
         },
         "call": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CallMeta"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "description": "Success",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": [
          "data",
          "result"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "data": {
           "type": "object",
           "properties": {
            "statementDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "\"the first statement ... under the requested week\", dd.MM.yyyy."
            },
            "statementDueDate": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "First due date under the requested week; \"the due date is statementDueDate here, not lastPayDate\"."
            },
            "statementDay": {
             "type": "integer",
             "description": "Statement day under the requested week."
            },
            "responseCode": {
             "type": "integer",
             "description": "\"responseCode 0 = fine.\""
            },
            "responseMessage": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "e.g. \"Success\"."
            }
           }
          },
          "result": {
           "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Result"
          }
         }
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "400": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/InvalidArguments"
     },
     "401": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
     },
     "500": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/TechnicalError"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "/statement.week.change": {
   "post": {
    "operationId": "statement.week.change",
    "summary": "Changes the card's statement week (side effect)",
    "description": "\"Call it only after the caller has agreed to the dates from 5.4.\" Contract suggests no automatic retry.",
    "requestBody": {
     "required": true,
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
         "data"
        ],
        "properties": {
         "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
           "cardNumber",
           "newStatementWeek",
           "statementDay"
          ],
          "properties": {
           "cardNumber": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Card number exactly as cards.list returned it."
           },
           "newStatementWeek": {
            "oneOf": [
             {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 4
             },
             {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
               "1",
               "2",
               "3",
               "4"
              ]
             }
            ],
            "description": "Requested week 1-4, number or string."
           },
           "statementDay": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "\"required by the request model even though the backend recalculates the day. Send the current day.\""
           }
          }
         },
         "call": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CallMeta"
         }
        }
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "description": "Success = exitState \"OK\" and responseCode 0",
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": [
          "data",
          "result"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "data": {
           "type": "object",
           "properties": {
            "responseCode": {
             "type": "integer",
             "description": "0 on success."
            },
            "responseMessage": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "e.g. \"00\"."
            },
            "statementWeek": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "New week, \"come back as strings here\"."
            },
            "statementDay": {
             "type": "string",
             "description": "\"Ignore statementDay in this answer\"."
            },
            "exitState": {
             "type": "string",
             "enum": [
              "OK"
             ],
             "description": "\"Success = exitState \\\"OK\\\" and responseCode 0.\""
            }
           }
          },
          "result": {
           "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Result"
          }
         }
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "400": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/InvalidArguments"
     },
     "401": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
     },
     "500": {
      "$ref": "#/components/responses/TechnicalError"
     }
    }
   }
  },
